{"name":"Fancy Flirt","hex":"#b4b780","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fancy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The imagination.","An image or representation of anything formed in the mind."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Decorative, or featuring decorations, especially intricate or diverse ones.","Of a superior grade."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fancy"},{"term":"flirt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sudden jerk; a quick throw or cast; a darting motion","Someone who flirts a lot or enjoys flirting; a flirtatious person."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To throw (something) with a jerk or sudden movement; to fling. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To jeer at; to mock."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flirt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flirting","blocks":[{"text":"Flirting, formally known as coquetry, is a form of social communication via body language, verbal expressions, or written language, intended to evoke feelings of playful excitement and potential romantic or sexual interest. Flirting can change in intention as well as intensity, whether it is performed for short-term fun or employed with a longer-term intention of seeking a romantic or sexual relationship."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Das_werdenSie_ja_nachher_schon_sehen.jpg/330px-Das_werdenSie_ja_nachher_schon_sehen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flirting"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Jealousy_and_Flirtation.jpg/500px-Jealousy_and_Flirtation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Jealousy_and_Flirtation.jpg/500px-Jealousy_and_Flirtation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A study in bo